* QH05TZ600  600 V, 5 A Qspeed H-series diode (Power Integrations)
* Datasheet-based model for ngspice. NOT a vendor model.
* Source: docs/datasheets/qh05tz600.pdf (Rev 1.3), typical values at 25 C.
* See prototype1/README.md for how each parameter was derived.
*
* The forward curve (Figure 3) has a knee near 1.2 V and a very soft slope.
* A plain SPICE diode can match it only with a large emission coefficient,
* and the large saturation current that goes with it would then show up as
* milliamps of reverse leakage. So the forward curve is a behavioural
* current source that conducts only when forward biased, and a parallel
* diode with negligible current carries the junction capacitance, the
* charge storage and the breakdown voltage.
*
* Pins: anode cathode
.subckt QH05TZ600 a k
BFWD a m I = V(a,m) > 0 ? 2.26m*(exp(min(V(a,m),6)/0.3128) - 1) : 0
DJ   a m QH05_J
RS   m k 37.8m
.model QH05_J D(is=1p n=12.1 cjo=41p vj=1 m=0.37 tt=1.3n bv=600 ibv=250u)
.ends QH05TZ600
